# Documentation Guidelines

### Documentation Best Practices

## Documentation Types
- API Documentation
- Code Comments
- README Files
- Architecture Diagrams
- User Guides
- Developer Guides
- Release Notes
- Troubleshooting Guides

## Documentation Checklist
- [ ] All public APIs documented
- [ ] Code comments are clear and useful
- [ ] README is up to date
- [ ] Architecture is documented
- [ ] Setup instructions are clear
- [ ] Configuration options documented
- [ ] Error messages are documented
- [ ] Examples are provided
- [ ] Version history maintained

## Code Documentation
- Document public interfaces
- Explain complex algorithms
- Document assumptions
- Include usage examples
- Note limitations
- Document dependencies
- Explain error handling
- Document configuration

## API Documentation
- Document endpoints
- List parameters
- Show examples
- Document responses
- Explain error codes
- Document authentication
- List rate limits
- Show versioning

## README Guidelines
- Project overview
- Installation steps
- Configuration options
- Usage examples
- Development setup
- Testing instructions
- Contributing guidelines
- License information

## Architecture Documentation
- System overview
- Component diagrams
- Data flow
- Integration points
- Security measures
- Performance considerations
- Scaling strategy
- Deployment process

## User Documentation
- Installation guide
- Configuration guide
- Usage instructions
- Troubleshooting guide
- FAQ section
- Known issues
- Support information
- Version history

## Documentation Maintenance
- Review regularly
- Update with changes
- Remove obsolete content
- Verify accuracy
- Check links
- Update examples
- Review formatting
- Validate completeness
